    "raw": "Given:\n- Ben spends 20% of his after-tax income on his car.\n- His car payment is $400.\n- He pays 1/3 of his gross income in taxes.\n\nFirst, let's find Ben's after-tax income. Since 20% of his after-tax income is $400, we can set up the equation:\n\\[ 0.20 \\times \\text{after-tax income} = 400 \\]\n\\[ \\text{after-tax income} = \\frac{400}{0.20} = 2000 \\]\n\nSo, Ben's after-tax income is $2000.\n\nNext, we need to find his gross income. We know that he pays 1/3 of his gross income in taxes, which means he keeps 2/3 of his gross income as after-tax income. Let \\( G \\) be his gross income. Then:\n\\[ \\frac{2}{3}G = 2000 \\]\n\\[ G = 2000 \\times \\frac{3}{2} = 3000 \\]\n\nSo, Ben's gross income before taxes is $3000.\n\nFINAL: 3000",
